# Crispy Baked Chicken Tenders

Based on [Yummy Toddler Food](https://www.yummytoddlerfood.com/baked-chicken-tenders) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251006230059/https://www.yummytoddlerfood.com/baked-chicken-tenders/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 pound [chicken tenders]{ ing="chicken-tenders" }
- [ ] [⅓ cup all-purpose flour]{ ing="cup-all-purpose-flour" } (or gluten-free flour)
- [ ] 2 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] 6 cups white or yellow [corn tortilla chips]{ ing="corn-tortilla-chips" } (or substitute 1 cup panko breadcrumbs)
- [ ] [¼ teaspoon salt]{ ing="teaspoon-salt" } (only if using panko instead of chips)

### For Serving

- [ ] [Ketchup]{ ing="ketchup" }
- [ ] [Ranch dressing]{ ing="ranch-dressing" }
- [ ] [Marinara sauce]{ ing="marinara-sauce" }
- [ ] [Applesauce]{ ing="applesauce" }
- [ ] [Honey mustard]{ ing="honey-mustard" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 425°F
1. Place a wire rack in a rimmed baking sheet and coat with nonstick cooking spray
1. If using [tortilla chips]{ ing="corn-tortilla-chips" }, pulse in food processor into fine crumbs (should yield about 1 cup). Pour into a shallow dish
1. Place [flour]{ ing="cup-all-purpose-flour" } in a second shallow dish
1. Beat [eggs]{ ing="egg" } lightly in a third shallow dish
1. Working with one [chicken tender]{ ing="chicken-tenders" } at a time, coat completely in [flour]{ ing="cup-all-purpose-flour" }, shaking off excess
1. Dip floured [tender]{ ing="chicken-tenders" } in beaten [egg]{ ing="egg" }, letting excess drip off
1. Press into [tortilla chip]{ ing="corn-tortilla-chips" } crumbs (or panko), coating all sides thoroughly
1. Arrange breaded [tenders]{ ing="chicken-tenders" } on the prepared wire rack without touching
1. Bake for 14-15 minutes until golden and fully cooked through (internal temperature 165°F)
1. Serve warm or at room temperature with your choice of dipping [sauces]{ ing="marinara-sauce" }

## Notes

- Using a wire rack is essential for achieving crispy results on all sides. Without it, the bottoms will be soggy
- Tortilla chips create a unique crunchy texture and add flavor. For panko version, add ¼ teaspoon salt to the flour before breading
- These are naturally kid-friendly and can be served with a variety of dipping sauces to suit different preferences
- Store leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days
- Reheat in a 350°F oven for 5-7 minutes to restore crispiness (avoid microwave which makes them soggy)
- Great for meal prep - bread all tenders, freeze unbaked on a baking sheet, then transfer to freezer bag. Bake from frozen, adding 3-5 minutes to cooking time
- Pairs well with sweet potato fries, roasted vegetables, or a simple side salad
- See [Kids Meal Adaptations](../reference/kids_meal_adaptations.dj) for more tips on making meals kid-friendly
